<article class="env-lemma" id="05VY">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05VY">Lemma <span data-tag="05VY">67.31.5</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$, $g : Y \to Z$ be morphisms of algebraic spaces over $S$. Let $\mathcal{G}$ be a quasi-coherent sheaf on $Y$. Let $x \in |X|$ with image $y \in |Y|$. If $f$ is flat at $x$, then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathcal{G}\text{ flat over }Z\text{ at }y \Leftrightarrow f^*\mathcal{G}\text{ flat over }Z\text{ at }x.  \]
</div>
  <p> In particular: If $f$ is surjective and flat, then $\mathcal{G}$ is flat over $Z$, if and only if $f^*\mathcal{G}$ is flat over $Z$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Pick a geometric point $\overline{x}$ of $X$ and denote $\overline{y}$ the image in $Y$ and $\overline{z}$ the image in $Z$. Via the characterization of flatness in Lemmas <a href="/tag/05VU" data-tag="05VU">67.31.1</a> and <a href="/tag/04NG" data-tag="04NG">67.30.8</a> and the description of the stalk of $f^*\mathcal{G}$ at $\overline{x}$ of Properties of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/05VQ" data-tag="05VQ">66.29.5</a> the lemma reduces to a purely algebraic question on the local ring maps $\mathcal{O}_{Z, \overline{z}} \to \mathcal{O}_{Y, \overline{y}} \to \mathcal{O}_{X, \overline{x}}$ and the module $\mathcal{G}_{\overline{y}}$. This algebraic statement is Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0584" data-tag="0584">10.39.9</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>